@7159. To "go out from Pharaoh" (Exodus 5:20) = when falsities did not so much infest.

@7404. "Moses and Aaron went out from before Pharaoh" (Exodus 8:12) = separation from those who reasoned from mere falsities. To "go out" = to be separated. @7650.

