@4006. "And all the she-goats speckled and spotted" (Genesis 30:35) = the goods thereof, in which evils and falsities were mixed. "She-goats" = the goods of truth; here, the goods adjoined to the truths treated of just above.

@4169. "Thy sheep and thy she-goats did not abort" (Genesis 31:38) = his state as to good and the good of truth... By the good of truth is meant the good of the understanding...

@4263. "Two hundred she-goats and twenty he-goats -capros-..." (Genesis 32:14) = Divine goods and truth thence derived. "She-goats" = goods; and "he-goats," truths; here, Divine ones.

@4769. See <Goat-Hircus>.

@7832. See <Cattle-Pecus>, pecudis.

@--. "A she-goat" = the innocence of the exterior man. References.

@7840. "From the lambs and from the she-goats ye shall take it" (Exodus 12:5) = the good of innocence exterior and interior... "A she-goat," or kid, = the good of truth in which there is innocence. References. That... "a kid," or "she-goat" the exterior good of innocence. References.

@9470. "Wool of she-goats" (Exodus 25:4) = good from the good of mutual love... (For) "a she-goat" = the good of innocence in the external or natural man... As it is not truth but good which is signified (by "wool"), in the Original Language, it is said "of she-goat," and not "wool of she-goats." Illustrated.

@9615. "Thou shalt make curtains with she-goats for a tent over the dwelling" (Exodus 26:7) = the external of Heaven which is from the truths which are from external celestial good... "The wool of she-goats" = external celestial good.

@9990[2]. The purifications of the internal man were represented by burnt-offerings and sacrifices from rams, kids, and she-goats; and that of the inmost internal man, by sacrifices from lambs.

@10042[8]. See <Goat-Capella>.

@DLW 346[2]. Perfect animals are... she-goats, etc.

@WE 1028. She-goats are of a middle kind between he-goats -hircos- and lambs; but approach more nearly to lambs, when by she-goats are meant kids.

