Good of Love.; Bonum amoris.
See <Celestial Good>, and see <Forehead>, <Mountain>, and <Oil>.

@AC 886. "Oil of olive"... = all the Celestial, thus all the good of love and of charity. Illustrated.

@1589[3]. For the good of love from the Lord continually inflows, through the internal man into the external; but the man who is in the affection of evil... perverts the good; but still the life thence remains. Explained. @7491. @7492.

@1824[end]. In proportion as the good of love and of charity is in the affection of good and the pleasure thence derived, it is celestial, and it is happy.

@2243[3]. (The decline of the Most Ancient Church from the good of love.)

@2256[2]. If he has lived in the goods of love and of charity, the Lord then separates evils, and through the goods with him elevates him into Heaven.

@2359. No one is admitted into... Heaven unless he is in the good of love and of charity; and no one can be in the good of love and of charity unless he acknowledges the Divine and the Holy of the Lord...

@2669[end]. The good of love is what makes the Celestial Church; and the good of faith, the Spiritual Church, The truth of faith does not make it, but introduces.

@2718[end]. In the good of love from the Lord there is celestial life; but not in the truth of faith separated thence.

@2761[5]. Under <Judah>, see this reference. @3654[6]. @4750. @9340[10].

@2826. Worship from the good of faith when the spiritual regenerate are treated of, and worship from the good of love when the celestial regenerate are treated of. Signified. @--[11].

