@267. I entered a certain grove, and there walked in meditation ...

@316. Being in rest and delight of mind... I saw afar a grove, in the middle of which was a porch...

@AE 160[2]. "The grove" which Ahab made = worship from falsities therefrom.

@391[14]. "Groves" = worship from spiritual things.

@--[23]. "Groves" = a religiosity from falsities.

@--[24]. "Groves with a green tree" (Jeremiah 17:2) = that worship from falsity.

@724[4]. Called "paradises" in the spiritual man; but "groves -luci et nemora-," in the natural; and "shady forests," in the sensuous.

