@CL 467. From causes truly weighty. @471. @474.

Guiltless.; Insons.

@AC 1834[2]. The Church... at the beginning is guiltless.

@5236. What is guiltless of the Church was rejected thither. Signified, Explained.

@--[2]. The reason "a boy" = what is guiltless, is that "an infant" = what is innocent;... but as with a boy innocence begins to be put off, "a boy" = that innocence which is called guiltless.

@5764. "And ye shall be guiltless" (Genesis 44:10) = that the rest shall be at their own disposal, because not at the same time in fault.

@8121. See <Guilt-Sons>.

@9029. "He that smiteth him shall be guiltless" (Exodus 21:19) = that he is not guilty -reum- of evil.

@9069. "The lord of the ox shall be guiltless" (Exodus 21:20) = that the evil is not from the internal man, because it is from the will and not from the understanding... "Guiltless" = without fault.

@9264. To "justify" = to declare guiltless, and to absolve. Illustrated.

@TCR 154[4]. See <Guilt-Reatus>.

@297. Jehovah will not hold him guiltless, who taketh His name in vain. General article.

@SE 3449. He desired to substitute the guiltless in his stead... @3455. @3465.

